    <description>Read by the AGS function 0x19084: with the gear code [0xFFFF915F] = 3 (dispatcher 0x190DC-0x1912A) and branch D ([0xFFFF917F] = 0) (test of [0xFFFF917F] = 1 at 0x191CC) it loads the catalog slot pointer 0x71BDE (lea 0x191EA) and for i = 1..3 ([0xFFFF915C]; the loop runs while i &lt; [0x70202] = 4, 0x1916E) calls the 2D8 lookup 0x19BD2 (jsr 0x191F6; 0x19BD2 -&gt; 0x19A90, bilinear interpolation): X = i (threshold index 1 / 2 / 3), Y = n_out/32 [0xFFFF9138] (written at 0x20D38: lsr 5, filtered output shaft speed). The byte result (interpolated Z) goes into a local array thr[i-1] (0x191FE). Then (0x192A4-0x192D2) the code walks i = 3 downward and takes the first (largest) i whose threshold is not above the pedal [0xFFFF912A] (= [0xFFFF911B], 0x1CDE6): [0xFFFF915D] = i + 1 (if none passes, [0xFFFF915D] = 1). So Z = pedal threshold (0-255) at which AGS level i + 1 is requested at that speed (column 1 = level 2, column 2 = level 3, column 3 = level 4). [0xFFFF915D] is compared with the current level [0xFFFF915B] (0x192E4-0x192E6): equal - the score drifts to the home scores 0x7089C; different - the matrix 0x708A8 / 0x708B8 changes the score [0xFFFF91D6] (row = [0xFFFF915D], column = [0xFFFF915B]); the score through the ladder 0x70898 (0x18EB8-0x18ED0) gives the level [0xFFFF915B], which selects the shift program through 0x09A42 (0x1ED8E: [0xFFFF87CC] = 0x09A42[[0xFFFF915B] - 1]). Axis Y: 62-125 (n_out = 32 x value, 1984-4000 rpm of the output shaft). Z array by Y rows: n_out/32 = 62: 153/230/252; n_out/32 = 77: 153/230/252; n_out/32 = 94: 153/230/252; n_out/32 = 105: 153/230/252; n_out/32 = 116: 153/230/252; n_out/32 = 125: 153/230/252. This table is used for: branch D ([0xFFFF917F] = 0); the paired table of the other branch is slot 8. The catalog label 'Y = pedal' is wrong: the pedal is the result (Z), axis Y is the output shaft speed. In the factory calibration this table is inactive: the AGS function 0x19084 is called from 0x18676 only when bit 5 of byte 0x70D39 is set (btst 0x18670, beq 0x18674), and in both 20C0 images (Alpina B3S reference and the car dump) 0x70D39 = 0x91, bit 5 = 0. The role is proven by code; the table affects the gearbox only if that bit is set (the 19D0 counterpart 0x8CE7 = 0xFD has bit 5 set). Inactive in the factory 20C0 calibration: function 0x19084 is called from 0x18676 only when bit 5 of byte 0x70D39 is set, and it holds 0x91 (bit 5 = 0).</description>
