  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x2038" flags="0x0">
    <title>AGS: score step when the pedal-requested level differs from the current level, branch D (pair of 0x708B8) (0x708A8)</title>
    <description>4x4 byte matrix read by the AGS function 0x19084 (movea 0x1939C, move.b (a0,d0.l) 0x193A2) when [0xFFFF917F] is not 1, i.e. in branch D (compare of (a2) with 1 at 0x19366-0x1936A; [0xFFFF917F] is written only at 0x1FE08 = 0 and at 0x1FE64 / 0x1FE96 / 0x1FEBE = 1; for 1 the pair 0x708B8 is read, 0x1937E). Index = ([0xFFFF915D] - 1) x 4 + ([0xFFFF915B] - 1) (0x1936C-0x1939A): ROW = [0xFFFF915D] (level requested by the pedal, slots 3-12), COLUMN = [0xFFFF915B] (current AGS level, 0x18ED0, from the score by the ladder 0x70898). Byte d7: below 0x80 - added to the score [0xFFFF91D6] saturating at 255 (jsr 0x14CB2, 0x193B0-0x193B6); 0x80 and above - subtract (256 - d7) saturating at 0 (jsr 0x14D4C, 0x193D6-0x193DC), but only if [0xFFFF9122] is not above [0x7029D] = 1 (0x193BA-0x193C6; [0xFFFF9122] is computed at 0x20110-0x20118 from the pedal rate of change [0xFFFF906E], exact scaling not analysed: a small value means an almost still pedal). Factory values (signed, minus = score decrease): row (pedal request) 1: 0/-21/-127/-127; row (pedal request) 2: 0/0/-65/-127; row (pedal request) 3: 0/0/0/-65; row (pedal request) 4: 0/0/0/0. All non-zero values lie where the requested level is below the current one (row less than column); on the diagonal and above they are zero: this matrix only lowers the score, score increase for a request above the current level is done elsewhere (not analysed here). The score [0xFFFF91D6] gives the level [0xFFFF915B] (ladder 0x70898, 0x18EB8-0x18ED0), the level selects the shift program through 0x09A42 (0x1ED8E-0x1ED94). Compared with 0x708B8: branch S steps are weaker (-17 / -33 / -65 vs -21 / -127). The axis labels of the catalog entry 0x708B8 (X = 'new step', Y = 'old step') are swapped: the column (X) is the current level [0xFFFF915B], the row (Y) is the requested level [0xFFFF915D]. In the factory calibration this table is inactive: the AGS function 0x19084 is called from 0x18676 only when bit 5 of byte 0x70D39 is set (btst 0x18670, beq 0x18674), and in both 20C0 images (Alpina B3S reference and the car dump) 0x70D39 = 0x91, bit 5 = 0. The role is proven by code; the table affects the gearbox only if that bit is set (the 19D0 counterpart 0x8CE7 = 0xFD has bit 5 set). Inactive in the factory 20C0 calibration: function 0x19084 is called from 0x18676 only when bit 5 of byte 0x70D39 is set, and it holds 0x91 (bit 5 = 0).</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="2" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>new step</units>
      <indexcount>4</indexcount>
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <LABEL index="0" value="0" />
      <LABEL index="1" value="1" />
      <LABEL index="2" value="2" />
      <LABEL index="3" value="3" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>old step</units>
      <indexcount>4</indexcount>
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <LABEL index="0" value="0" />
      <LABEL index="1" value="1" />
      <LABEL index="2" value="2" />
      <LABEL index="3" value="3" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="z">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x708A8" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedrowcount="4" mmedcolcount="4" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
      <units>AGS score step per tick: signed byte, below 0x80 plus, 0x80 and above minus (256 - value); minus applies when [0xFFFF9122] is not above 1</units>
