  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x205B" flags="0x0">
    <title>Line B check (error 0x2D = 45): threshold of the difference A - B, factory 1000 mV (0x70F50)</title>
    <description>Voltage channels: [0xFFFF8FFE] (A) = ADC 0xFFFF8A06 x 25250 / 1024, mV (written at 0x1C4C4); [0xFFFF9000] (B) = ADC 0xFFFF8A08 x 25250 / 1024, mV (written at 0x1C47A); no other writers. Read by function 0x233DA (19D0 pair 0x26ED8) in state [0xFFFF8C0E] = 1: d0 = [0xFFFF8FFE] - [0x70F50] (sub.w 0x233F4), then cmp.w with [0xFFFF9000] (0x233FA-0x23400): condition 'A - 1000 &gt; B'. If it holds and [0xFFFF9000] &gt; [0x70F54] (0x2340C-0x23416), the flag d7 = 0, otherwise d7 = 1; d7 is passed as the c(a6) argument to the error registration 0x1534C with code 45 (0x2D) (jsr 0x23428); for d7 not 0 after the registration [0xFFFF8FC8] = 3 or 2 (0x23442 / 0x23448), state [0xFFFF8C0E] = 2 (0x2344C). Which outcome of the check means a fault (polarity of the c(a6) argument of 0x1534C) is not established. The value 1000 is not the 'tolerance between the supply lines' (that tolerance is 0x70F46 = 1500, 0x228C0): it takes part only in the code 45 check. There are no other references to this address in the image (32-bit value search over the whole image). </description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="13" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x70F50" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>mV (difference A - B, 25.25 V scale channels)</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x205C" flags="0x0">
    <title>Supply voltage window, upper limit, factory 16000 mV (0x70F52)</title>
    <description>Voltage channels: [0xFFFF8FFE] (A) = ADC 0xFFFF8A06 x 25250 / 1024, mV (written at 0x1C4C4); [0xFFFF9000] (B) = ADC 0xFFFF8A08 x 25250 / 1024, mV (written at 0x1C47A); no other writers. Read at 0x1B120 (cmp.w, start-up check 0x1B106, 19D0 pair 0x1FB3E): in state [0xFFFF8648] = 1 (0x1B10E), when [0xFFFF8FFE] &gt; [0x70F56] (0x1B118, bls 0x1B11E) and [0xFFFF8FFE] &lt; [0x70F52] (0x1B120, bcc 0x1B126), it writes [0xFFFF8648] = 2 (0x1B128). State 2 is the last condition of the supply self-test: [0xFFFF8648] is set to 1 at 0x1B478 once the other tests are ready (0x1B43C-0x1B470), and with [0xFFFF8648] = 2 and [0xFFFF86CC] = 2 the chain 0x1B47A-0x1B48E sets [0xFFFF8592] = 1; [0xFFFF8592] = 0 holds the gear [0xFFFF915F] = 4 (0x19572-0x195A8, branch 0). Result: outside the 9.0-16.0 V window [0xFFFF8648] does not reach 2 and the transmission start-up does not continue. Not a temperature. There are no other references to this address in the image (32-bit value search over the whole image). </description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="13" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x70F52" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>mV ([0xFFFF8FFE] strictly below)</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x205D" flags="0x0">
    <title>Line B check (error 0x2D = 45): threshold of the voltage B [0xFFFF9000], factory 2500 mV (0x70F54)</title>
    <description>Voltage channels: [0xFFFF8FFE] (A) = ADC 0xFFFF8A06 x 25250 / 1024, mV (written at 0x1C4C4); [0xFFFF9000] (B) = ADC 0xFFFF8A08 x 25250 / 1024, mV (written at 0x1C47A); no other writers. Read by three steps of the code 45 (0x2D) check: 0x233DA (movea 0x23402, cmp 0x2340E and 0x23438; state [0xFFFF8C0E]), 0x23456 (cmp 0x234AC and 0x234BC; state [0xFFFF8C10]), 0x234EC (cmp 0x23536 and 0x2355A; state [0xFFFF8C12]). Operand: [0xFFFF9000] (B). Sinks: the flag d7 as the c(a6) argument of the error registration 0x1534C with code 45 (jsr 0x23428, 0x234D6, 0x23574) and the state word [0xFFFF8FC8] (0x23442 = 3 for B below 2500, 0x23448 = 2; 0x234B4 = 0; 0x234E0 / 0x2357E = 4; 0x2353E = 0), which is read by the self-test step 0x1B340 ([0xFFFF8FC8] = 4 -&gt; [0xFFFF863E] = 2), 0x1B37C-0x1B3B2 and the output stage check 0x106D8 (0x10736: [0xFFFF8FC8] = 3 and [0xFFFF8FFE] x 80 / 100 not above [0xFFFF9000] -&gt; d7 = 1 into the registration of error 0x2E = 46, jsr 0x10770). Which outcome of the check means a fault (polarity of the c(a6) argument of 0x1534C) is not established. What is physically connected to the ADC 0xFFFF8A08 (line B) is not established; the same compares use 0x8EFE in 19D0. There are no other references to this address in the image (32-bit value search over the whole image). </description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="13" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x70F54" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>mV (channel B, 25.25 V scale)</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x205E" flags="0x0">
    <title>Supply voltage window, lower limit, factory 9000 mV (0x70F56)</title>
    <description>Voltage channels: [0xFFFF8FFE] (A) = ADC 0xFFFF8A06 x 25250 / 1024, mV (written at 0x1C4C4); [0xFFFF9000] (B) = ADC 0xFFFF8A08 x 25250 / 1024, mV (written at 0x1C47A); no other writers. Read at 0x1B118 (cmp.w) in the same check 0x1B106 as 0x70F52: for [0xFFFF8FFE] not above [0x70F56] (bls 0x1B11E) the state [0xFFFF8648] does not go to 2. Sink and consequences are the same as for 0x70F52 (0x1B128, 0x1B478-0x1B48E, 0x19572-0x195A8). Not '90 C'. There are no other references to this address in the image (32-bit value search over the whole image). </description>
