  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x205F" flags="0x0">
    <title>Sensor on [0xFFFF9014] / [0xFFFF9016]: 'both near 2.5 V' window, top, factory 2700 mV (0x70F5E)</title>
    <description>Two analog inputs [0xFFFF9014] and [0xFFFF9016] are written by 0x1C528 (19D0 pair 0x20E6C) from a buffer whose address is stored in ROM at 0xA2D4: buffer words +2 and +4, value x 5000 / 1024, mV (0x1C56A, 0x1C596: muls.l #$1388, divs.l #$400). The difference [0xFFFF9012] = max([0xFFFF9016] - [0xFFFF9014], 0) (jsr 0x14CF0 at 0x1C59E, store 0x1C5AA) goes into the 1D16 table of slot 41 (0x71C66, jsr 0x199A2) -&gt; [0xFFFF8C8C] -&gt; low byte of [0xFFFF9066] (ATF temperature sensor per document 11 section 8; 0x1C610). The monitor 0x236E2 (19D0 pair 0x271E0; its address is in the ROM tables 0xA46E, 0xA68A, 0xA7F8) registers an error with code 5 through jsr 0x1534C (0x2398A), class in d1 = d7 (0 - both channels inside the 2.3-2.7 V window; 2, 3, 4 - combinations of exceeding 0x70F64 and 0x70F68; 1 - check of the change of [0xFFFF8C8C] against [0xFFFF9067] with the tolerance [0x70116], 0x23914-0x23940). Code 5 is also read at 0x1CDB6 (jsr 0x1532A) as the condition to replace the pedal [0xFFFF911B] by the table 0x19F42 (0x1CDCC-0x1CDE4); the relation of that use to the sensor on [0xFFFF9014] / [0xFFFF9016] is not established. Read by 0x236E2 at 0x238B4 (for [0xFFFF9016]) and 0x238CA (for [0xFFFF9014]): both channels must be strictly below 0x70F5E and strictly above 0x70F60 (0x238BC / 0x238D2), then the class d7 = 0 (0x238DA) and error 5 of class 0 goes to 0x1534C. Matches 19D0 0x8F08. Not '27 C'. There are no other references to this address in the image (32-bit value search over the whole image). </description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="13" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x70F5E" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>mV (5 V scale)</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <outputtype>1</outputtype>
    <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x2060" flags="0x0">
    <title>Sensor on [0xFFFF9014] / [0xFFFF9016]: 'both near 2.5 V' window, bottom, factory 2300 mV (0x70F60)</title>
    <description>Two analog inputs [0xFFFF9014] and [0xFFFF9016] are written by 0x1C528 (19D0 pair 0x20E6C) from a buffer whose address is stored in ROM at 0xA2D4: buffer words +2 and +4, value x 5000 / 1024, mV (0x1C56A, 0x1C596: muls.l #$1388, divs.l #$400). The difference [0xFFFF9012] = max([0xFFFF9016] - [0xFFFF9014], 0) (jsr 0x14CF0 at 0x1C59E, store 0x1C5AA) goes into the 1D16 table of slot 41 (0x71C66, jsr 0x199A2) -&gt; [0xFFFF8C8C] -&gt; low byte of [0xFFFF9066] (ATF temperature sensor per document 11 section 8; 0x1C610). The monitor 0x236E2 (19D0 pair 0x271E0; its address is in the ROM tables 0xA46E, 0xA68A, 0xA7F8) registers an error with code 5 through jsr 0x1534C (0x2398A), class in d1 = d7 (0 - both channels inside the 2.3-2.7 V window; 2, 3, 4 - combinations of exceeding 0x70F64 and 0x70F68; 1 - check of the change of [0xFFFF8C8C] against [0xFFFF9067] with the tolerance [0x70116], 0x23914-0x23940). Code 5 is also read at 0x1CDB6 (jsr 0x1532A) as the condition to replace the pedal [0xFFFF911B] by the table 0x19F42 (0x1CDCC-0x1CDE4); the relation of that use to the sensor on [0xFFFF9014] / [0xFFFF9016] is not established. Read by 0x236E2 at 0x238BC (for [0xFFFF9016]) and 0x238D2 (for [0xFFFF9014]): lower bound of the window (the value must be strictly above), pair of 0x70F5E. Matches 19D0 0x8F0A. Not '23 C'. There are no other references to this address in the image (32-bit value search over the whole image). </description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="13" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x70F60" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
