  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x2061" flags="0x0">
    <title>ATF sensor: upper limit of the accepted difference [0xFFFF9012], factory 2504 mV (0x70F62)</title>
    <description>Two analog inputs [0xFFFF9014] and [0xFFFF9016] are written by 0x1C528 (19D0 pair 0x20E6C) from a buffer whose address is stored in ROM at 0xA2D4: buffer words +2 and +4, value x 5000 / 1024, mV (0x1C56A, 0x1C596: muls.l #$1388, divs.l #$400). The difference [0xFFFF9012] = max([0xFFFF9016] - [0xFFFF9014], 0) (jsr 0x14CF0 at 0x1C59E, store 0x1C5AA) goes into the 1D16 table of slot 41 (0x71C66, jsr 0x199A2) -&gt; [0xFFFF8C8C] -&gt; low byte of [0xFFFF9066] (ATF temperature sensor per document 11 section 8; 0x1C610). Read at 0x1C608 (cmp.w, function 0x1C528) in the branch 'error 6 not active' (jsr 0x1532A with d0 = 6 at 0x1C5C6, beq 0x1C5FE): [0xFFFF9012] must be not below 0x70F66 = 1014 (0x1C600, bcs 0x1C614) and not above 0x70F62 (0x1C608, bhi 0x1C614); only then [0xFFFF9066] = low byte of [0xFFFF8C8C] (0x1C610); outside 1014-2504 mV [0xFFFF9066] keeps its old value (the part of the slot 41 table between 2504 and 2673 mV does not reach [0xFFFF9066]). [0xFFFF9066] is read, among others, by 0x1CE30 ([0xFFFF906A] = [0xFFFF9066] + 8) and 0x228D0 (table 0x70F32 in the voltage monitor). Matches 19D0 0x8F0C. There are no other references to this address in the image (32-bit value search over the whole image). </description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="13" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x70F62" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>mV ([0xFFFF9012], 5 V scale)</units>
