  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x2062" flags="0x0">
    <title>Sensor on [0xFFFF9014] / [0xFFFF9016]: upper threshold of channel [0xFFFF9016], factory 4500 mV (0x70F64)</title>
    <description>Two analog inputs [0xFFFF9014] and [0xFFFF9016] are written by 0x1C528 (19D0 pair 0x20E6C) from a buffer whose address is stored in ROM at 0xA2D4: buffer words +2 and +4, value x 5000 / 1024, mV (0x1C56A, 0x1C596: muls.l #$1388, divs.l #$400). The difference [0xFFFF9012] = max([0xFFFF9016] - [0xFFFF9014], 0) (jsr 0x14CF0 at 0x1C59E, store 0x1C5AA) goes into the 1D16 table of slot 41 (0x71C66, jsr 0x199A2) -&gt; [0xFFFF8C8C] -&gt; low byte of [0xFFFF9066] (ATF temperature sensor per document 11 section 8; 0x1C610). The monitor 0x236E2 (19D0 pair 0x271E0; its address is in the ROM tables 0xA46E, 0xA68A, 0xA7F8) registers an error with code 5 through jsr 0x1534C (0x2398A), class in d1 = d7 (0 - both channels inside the 2.3-2.7 V window; 2, 3, 4 - combinations of exceeding 0x70F64 and 0x70F68; 1 - check of the change of [0xFFFF8C8C] against [0xFFFF9067] with the tolerance [0x70116], 0x23914-0x23940). Code 5 is also read at 0x1CDB6 (jsr 0x1532A) as the condition to replace the pedal [0xFFFF911B] by the table 0x19F42 (0x1CDCC-0x1CDE4); the relation of that use to the sensor on [0xFFFF9014] / [0xFFFF9016] is not established. Read by 0x236E2 at 0x2384E, 0x23870, 0x23892 (cmp.w [0xFFFF9016] with 0x70F64) together with the threshold 0x70F68 = 500 for [0xFFFF9014]: [0xFFFF9016] &gt; 4500 and [0xFFFF9014] &gt; 500 - class 2 (0x23864); [0xFFFF9016] &lt; 4500 and [0xFFFF9014] &lt; 500 - class 3 (0x23886); [0xFFFF9016] &gt; 4500 and [0xFFFF9014] &lt; 500 - class 4 (0x238A8). The class goes into d1 of the error 5 registration (jsr 0x1534C, 0x2398A). Matches 19D0 0x8F0E. There are no other references to this address in the image (32-bit value search over the whole image). </description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="13" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x70F64" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
